00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:31.950
Like he's just being really
sweet in front of my kids.

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:35.100
And it wasn't until he said,
I'm missing just one thing.

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:38.250
I was like, oh, this is really
about to happen right now.

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:39.667
Like he's about to pull out a ring.

00:01:39.667 --> 00:01:40.958
- [Kelly] Aw, that is so sweet.

00:01:40.958 --> 00:01:42.540
- So I don't dunno. I
think it was a tossup.

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:45.030
- And Austin, did you write
the book that you're reading?

00:01:45.030 --> 00:01:46.950
- Yeah. So the Strike Zone

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:49.770
is an Austin Dunwoody original, actually.

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:52.530
I wrote it in my prime in third grade.

00:01:52.530 --> 00:01:54.330
The point of the book

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:57.210
as third graders think
I actually turned into a

00:01:57.210 --> 00:01:58.740
